# 2. NON-NEGOTIABLE RULE

Everything that is presented as a scientific result must come from actual computation over real data.

Never:

- hard-code fake measurements
- invent source coordinates
- invent flux values
- invent uncertainties
- invent confidence scores
- invent catalog matches
- invent archive responses
- generate fake FITS metadata
- display synthetic images as real observations
- silently fall back to demo data
- claim an algorithm ran when it did not
- claim a discovery that has not been scientifically established

If a feature cannot be completed correctly, expose that limitation clearly.

Do NOT replace a missing scientific implementation with a fake result just to make the UI look complete.

