# 13. FITS PROCESSING

Use Astropy or another scientifically appropriate maintained library.

The system must inspect the actual FITS structure rather than assuming a fixed layout.

Record:

- product identifier
- filename
- source URL
- checksum
- data release
- observation date/time
- image dimensions
- data type
- units
- WCS
- available science extensions
- quality/flag information
- variance information
- relevant calibration metadata

Validate all of these.

If a required field is missing:

DO NOT GUESS.

Report:

**"This measurement cannot be calculated reliably from this product."**

---

# 14. WCS

Use the actual WCS information contained in the FITS products.

Validate:

- coordinate transformation
- image footprint
- orientation
- pixel scale
- compatibility between observations

Use appropriate reprojection methods when required.

Track:

- transformation
- interpolation
- registration quality
- invalid regions

Do not assume that two images are directly comparable merely because they cover the same sky location.

---

# 15. IMAGE COMPATIBILITY

